class: abi
profiles: standard
summary: platform/libc's lock numbers and struct flock, struct winsize, struct passwd and struct group, TCSA timings and O_NOCTTY and AT_SYMLINK_FOLLOW, each system's terminal record, modes and window requests, the kernel's struct termios, requests and statx flags on Linux and F_FULLFSYNC on Darwin, each held to the system's own C headers; a file platform/posix makes and gives permission bits and times, and a link to it, read the same through C's stat and readlink, and root's account and group zero read through platform/posix as the C library's own lookups give them
